cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Engagement Probe: predicting how fully a language model will answer, from its pre-answer internal state"
abstract: >-
  A two-round study, with the protocol frozen and hash-recorded before data
  collection, testing whether an instruction-tuned language
  model's hidden state, recorded after it reads a prompt but before it generates
  any tokens, predicts how substantively it will engage with that request. On an
  untouched confirmation split the activation probe reached Spearman 0.868
  against 0.822 for a sparse prompt-text baseline; the +0.046 advantage did not
  clear the prespecified decision rule, and the primary result is reported as
  inconclusive. Includes the frozen protocol, the prompt set, three-judge
  blinded ratings, and the released Round 2 data.
type: software
